vices is unknown. These are recorded observations from named sources — an inventory, not a census or an estimate (SIG-METRIC-008). A resolved site is a cluster of records judged to describe the same physical device: 0 same-device merges were auto-written (only tiers whose measured holdout precision cleared the published floor) and 0 were accepted in human review under the same hard constraints; 0 proposed merges still await review and are not counted, 0 reviewer rejects are recorded as cannot-link and 0 accepted merges were refused by the hard constraints — none of these cluster. Resolution rests on a provisional eval (LLM-bootstrapped gold set; D-R6.1-EVAL, OPEN).","rights":{"attribution":"© The SIG project — CC-BY-4.0","attribution_required":true,"license":"CC-BY-4.0","share_alike":false,"source_id":"sig","terms_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","upstream_license":null},"value":"3 resolved sites (from 3 observation-level records; dedup ratio 0.000)"}]}
